  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financing and Integrating Renewable Energy for the City of Butuan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippine government is seeking to increase the proportion of renewable energy and use them to reduce energy costs and greenhouse gas emissions. The project supported these goals by further developing the financing and integration of renewable energy in the city of Butuan. Various urban stakeholders were working together in a Planning Group for Energy Development with the aim of developing an inclusive, cost-effective and sustainable energy solution. A development plan for urban energy development ensured that domestic, renewable resources will be used in line with the development goals. To achieve this, the stakeholders completed a workshop series on various aspects relevant to planning in the energy sector. Armed with this newly-acquired knowledge, they can technically and financially evaluate the proposals for energy development. The project also looked at financial instruments that will contribute to the implementation of the development plan.</narrative>
  </description>
